#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073415 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073793 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "940366ef-28e8-5827-b52d-a8b500dbb2a1" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Fraction by a Whole Number: Result Is a Mixed Number"}] :question/id #uuid "3deda9a1-7edd-5b1e-9f39-5c69644f30ab" :question/math-academy-id "e-10542" :question/problem "Greg stacked $5$ cardboard boxes on top of each other. How tall was his pile if each box is $\\dfrac{3}{4}\\,\\textrm{ft}$ high?" :question/worked-solution "To find out the height of the pile of boxes, we have to multiply $\\dfrac{3}{4}$ by $5.$\n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n5 \\times \\dfrac34 = \\dfrac{5\\times 3}{4} = \\dfrac{15}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert $\\dfrac {15}{4}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n15 \\div 4 = 3\\,\\textrm{R}\\,3 = 3\\,\\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nSo, Greg's stack of boxes was $3\\,\\dfrac{3}{4}\\,\\textrm{ft}$ high."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073416 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b58f3a78-53b1-577f-8907-d53a00186686" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whole Number Bounds of a Multiplication Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "9fb671f7-6d04-5863-9683-3b2c3753df73" :question/math-academy-id "e-10543" :question/problem "Mr. Stewart spends $\\dfrac56$ hours watching an episode of his favorite TV show. If $5$ episodes are played every week, find the total time he spends watching the show every week. Between what two whole numbers does your answer lie?" :question/worked-solution "To find out how long Mr. Stewart watches the show each week, we need to multiply $\\dfrac{5}{6}$ by $5.$ \n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n5\\times\\dfrac56 = \\dfrac{5\\times 5}{6} = \\dfrac{25}6\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert $\\dfrac {25}{6}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n25 \\div 6 = 4\\,\\textrm{R}\\,1 = 4\\,\\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSo, Mr. Stewart spends a total of  $4\\,\\dfrac{1}{6}$ hours watching the show, which lies between $4$ and $5$ hours."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073538 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073859 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8b003cb-5504-549c-8da4-fdc91242c8af" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Fraction by a Whole Number: Result Is a Whole Number"}] :question/id #uuid "737b03c4-95f0-5a89-a428-e051b9efee6d" :question/math-academy-id "e-1863" :question/problem "Larry filled his water bottle with $12\\, \\mathrm{oz}$ of drinking water. If he drank $\\dfrac34$ of the bottle's contents after exercising, how much water did Larry drink?" :question/worked-solution "To find out how much water Larry drank, we need to multiply $12$ by $\\dfrac{3}{4}.$\n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac34 \\times 12 = \\dfrac{3\\times 12}{4} = \\dfrac{36}4\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{36}{4} = 36 \\div 4=9\n$$\n\nSo, Larry drank $9\\,\\textrm{oz}$ of water."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073793 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "940366ef-28e8-5827-b52d-a8b500dbb2a1" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Fraction by a Whole Number: Result Is a Mixed Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77271cf0-1700-50f0-a95f-47ec28a0b327" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455122} {:answer/id #uuid "7c0d3ca0-81d4-5cc1-a340-6764642d8e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455131} {:answer/id #uuid "7c760560-8cf8-50aa-aa43-9d2bdeabd9d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455132} {:answer/id #uuid "98240ed4-7955-5e04-9b6c-42bf3125c1f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455179} {:answer/id #uuid "a6a06d2f-1db7-5122-a5c5-f860c4b0e5d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77271cf0-1700-50f0-a95f-47ec28a0b327" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455122} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7542c69-109b-5a14-9394-be91f8d9c21a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455415}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "69f7ec22-029d-5e0b-8220-6e82cfcbf15b" :question/math-academy-id "q-150234" :question/problem "An electrician takes a $4$-meter-long electrical cable from which he has to cut a piece that is $\\frac{5}{6}$ of its length. How long will that piece be?" :question/worked-solution "To find out the length of the piece to be cut, we need to multiply $4$ by $\\frac{5}{6}.$  \n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}\\times 4=\\frac{5\\times 4}{6}=\\frac{20}{6}\n$$\n\nWe then reduce this fraction to its lowest terms:\n\n$$\n\\frac{20}{6}=\\frac{20÷2}{6÷2}=\\frac{10}{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we then convert $\\frac{10}{3}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n10÷3=3\\,\\text{R}\\,1=3\\,\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the piece will be $3\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{m}$ long."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b58f3a78-53b1-577f-8907-d53a00186686" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whole Number Bounds of a Multiplication Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06c2ab15-bc8d-5ba8-b327-fb9615b9f13a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Between $2$ and $3$ miles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454922} {:answer/id #uuid "2411e9aa-dd89-55ac-a734-a79032efee86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Between $1$ and $2$ miles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454959} {:answer/id #uuid "43fb878d-08a7-500f-bce4-2258d362584d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Between $4$ and $5$ miles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455018} {:answer/id #uuid "8f22ff0a-29dd-50dd-908d-a55d673a687e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Between $5$ and $6$ miles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455161} {:answer/id #uuid "d57d0ade-4bfc-5eb8-a546-b1daf524098e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Between $3$ and $4$ miles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43fb878d-08a7-500f-bce4-2258d362584d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Between $4$ and $5$ miles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455018} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cb58f82-99fa-5ce0-9863-9af9bd19cb81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "963a7b5f-c364-5634-90c3-78590b2f0ada" :question/math-academy-id "q-150345" :question/problem "George rides his bike $\\frac{9}{10}$ of a mile each day, going from home to school and back. Compute how many miles he rides in $5$ days just by going to school and back. Between what two whole numbers does your answer lie?" :question/worked-solution "To find out how many kilometers George travels in $5$ days just by going to school and back, we have to multiply $\\frac{9}{10}$ by $5.$\n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n5\\times \\frac{9}{10}=\\frac{5\\times 9}{10}=\\frac{45}{10}\n$$\n\nWe then reduce this fraction to its lowest terms:\n\n$$\n\\frac{45}{10}=\\frac{45÷5}{10÷5}=\\frac{9}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert $\\frac{9}{2}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n9÷2=4\\,\\text{R}\\,1=4\\,\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, in $5$ days, George rides a total of $4\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{mi},$ which lies between $4$ and $5$ miles."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455461 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b58f3a78-53b1-577f-8907-d53a00186686" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whole Number Bounds of a Multiplication Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "050d3e56-54e6-5b8c-b391-5e2c8b18f3b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Between $8$ and $9$ pages" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454916} {:answer/id #uuid "32c2df8c-663e-5302-8bfa-5f7afcdd5ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Between $6$ and $7$ pages" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454980} {:answer/id #uuid "aceebc6a-32c2-5168-b688-80daacda9264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Between $4$ and $5$ pages" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455206} {:answer/id #uuid "c51d793f-e0e8-5792-9d54-c4f10f6049d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Between $7$ and $8$ pages" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218645