umerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{8}\\times 8=\\frac{7\\times 8}{8}=\\frac{56}{8}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{56}{8}=56÷8=7\n$$\n\nSo, Theresa poured $7$ cups of orange juice from the jug."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074431 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073859 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8b003cb-5504-549c-8da4-fdc91242c8af" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Fraction by a Whole Number: Result Is a Whole Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37742470-e3c8-5fb9-a6e6-b72a6f2e8fbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{lb}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454990} {:answer/id #uuid "4f9f6322-8f7a-5dfb-87e3-764efb020c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{lb}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455044} {:answer/id #uuid "6b0f059b-fb59-58a3-8e67-b052578ab45f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{lb}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455100} {:answer/id #uuid "af25461e-30f1-573b-944b-2831ae10f792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{lb}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455210} {:answer/id #uuid "ce170244-053a-5d94-b63f-5dc3bd792d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}\\,\\text{lb}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af25461e-30f1-573b-944b-2831ae10f792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{lb}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455210} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0260df7-3f28-567d-be7b-5a8248ccc368" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186072824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "742b3068-cb41-500e-9a85-dc782f036323" :question/math-academy-id "q-60319" :question/problem "Ted made pizzas for his soccer buddies. He put $\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{lb}$ of cheese on each pizza. If he made $8$ pizzas, how many pounds of cheese did he use in total?" :question/worked-solution "To find out how much cheese Ted used, we need to multiply $\\frac{1}{4}$ by $8.$\n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n8\\times \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{8\\times 1}{4}=\\frac{8}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{4}=8÷4=2\n$$\n\nSo, Ted used $2\\,\\text{lb}$ of cheese to make the pizzas."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073793 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "940366ef-28e8-5827-b52d-a8b500dbb2a1" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Fraction by a Whole Number: Result Is a Mixed Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b0d9a1a-27d2-5952-9795-47855f250dc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\frac{3}{8}\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455065} {:answer/id #uuid "6541334d-ec6b-5266-a8f5-3cc6bec15db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455087} {:answer/id #uuid "678a6e45-e483-51a9-8dd3-69405cb5a593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\frac{7}{8}\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455092} {:answer/id #uuid "88151c68-7843-570d-b09e-c1c88c15837c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\frac{3}{8}\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455147} {:answer/id #uuid "8ddd1b93-3180-52bf-bf8c-30d66a7aa5cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\frac{5}{8}\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "678a6e45-e483-51a9-8dd3-69405cb5a593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\frac{7}{8}\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455092} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb075ecd-d667-5628-a59c-aab6c1c53a3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186072908}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7aec9a99-287b-5359-b077-2d2284acc8d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-60472" :question/problem "A wooden slat is $3\\,\\text{ft}$ long. Eddie needs to cut a piece that's $\\frac{5}{8}$ the length of the slat. How long is the piece he has to cut?" :question/worked-solution "To find the length of the piece that Eddie has to cut, we have to multiply $3$ by $\\frac{5}{8}.$  \n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{8}\\times 3=\\frac{5\\times 3}{8}=\\frac{15}{8}\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert $\\frac{15}{8}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n15÷8=1\\,\\text{R}\\,7=1\\,\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$\n\nSo, Eddie has to cut a piece $1\\,\\frac{7}{8}\\,\\text{ft}$ long."}]}
